self_use_verifiable_task
  record_type "benchmark_suite"
  id "issue_1138_self_use_verifiable_task"
  title "Wave F self-use observations: verifiable task routing (plan 08)"
  purpose "Issue #1138 plan 14 wave F. Thirty held-out prompts from data/benchmarks/verifiable-task-paraphrases.lino were given to Formal AI through the real `@link-assistant/agent` CLI and through `formal-ai chat`, and what came back was recorded. This file holds the expected answer and the observed outcome per family; the prompts themselves stay in the plan 08 corpus so there is one copy of each held-out string. Raw transcripts: docs/case-studies/issue-1138/self-use/."
  runner "cargo test --test unit issue_1138_self_use_verifiable_task"
  report_mode "Per-family expected value and observed outcome with the binary version and commit that produced it. An expectation is never weakened; a family moves to `observed_pass` only when a re-run produces the expected answer."
  prompts_from "data/benchmarks/verifiable-task-paraphrases.lino"
  topic "verifiable_task / derivation versus retrieval"
  observed_with "formal-ai 0.350.0"
  observed_at_commit "dc9b0574607a26f3e1c8bdb8ce93c0c7f786f197"
  family_count "6"
  language_count "5"
self_use_expectation_arithmetic_narrative
  record_type "benchmark_expectation"
  id "arithmetic_narrative"
  plan "08"
  expected_answer "3"
  derivation "24 + 18 = 42; 42 - 35 = 7; 7 - 4 = 3"
  requirement "A multi-step arithmetic narrative is a verifiable task: the answer is derived and the derivation is executed (plan 08, `the_composed_program_is_executed_and_its_output_is_the_answer`)."
  observed "Not derived in any language. Through the Agent CLI the English prompt was sent to `websearch` and the system tried to open a homework-answer page for the same word problem; the fetch returned 403 and the run ended offering to file an issue report. Through `chat` four languages answer with the web-search capability description and Spanish with the unknown-language fallback. Looking for someone else's answer to a word problem is not derivation."
  outcome "wrong_route"
  languages_correct "0"
self_use_expectation_counted_category
  record_type "benchmark_expectation"
  id "counted_category"
  plan "08"
  expected_answer "5"
  derivation "stethoscope x1 + scalpel x3 + thermometer x1; oboe and harp are not medical instruments"
  requirement "Counting with multiplicity over a category the seed does not carry, in all five languages (plan 08, `multiplicity_is_attached_to_its_entity`)."
  observed "English answers `5`, exactly and with nothing else — the one solved task of this pass, and it requires category membership the seed does not hold. The same prompt in Russian is sent to `websearch` instead and ends in an empty conversation-summary scaffold after three unrelated fetches; Hindi and Chinese get the capability description; Spanish gets the unknown-language fallback. The capability exists and is reachable in exactly one language."
  outcome "solved_in_one_language_of_five"
  languages_correct "1"
self_use_expectation_instructed_edit
  record_type "benchmark_expectation"
  id "instructed_edit"
  plan "08"
  expected_answer "a shorter sentence with the same meaning"
  requirement "An instructed text edit with an unquoted operand must edit the operand the prompt supplies (plan 08 case 3)."
  observed "English is read as a shell command — ``It looks like you want to run a terminal command`` — and declined for lack of Agent mode. Russian asks a clarifying question about which program or result to change, so the edit route assumes a program operand rather than the sentence in the prompt. Chinese and Spanish get the web-search capability description."
  outcome "wrong_route"
  languages_correct "0"
self_use_expectation_named_unknown
  record_type "benchmark_expectation"
  id "named_unknown"
  plan "08"
  expected_answer "12"
  derivation "7 * y = 84; y = 84 / 7 = 12"
  forbidden_answer "29"
  requirement "A named unknown with a colon declaration is solved, not routed elsewhere (plan 08 case 4, the `Find x:` misroute)."
  observed "The worst outcome of the pass. Through the Agent CLI the English prompt is sent to `websearch`, three algebra sites are fetched, and the raw scraped text of one of them is emitted into the answer channel — including the string `y=29`, which is the solution to a different equation that happened to be on the page. The answer to the prompt is 12. A wrong number lifted from an unrelated problem reached the answer channel with no derivation and no check. Through `chat` the English prompt is instead read as a terminal command."
  outcome "wrong_answer_scraped"
  languages_correct "0"
self_use_expectation_unit_conversion
  record_type "benchmark_expectation"
  id "unit_conversion"
  plan "08"
  expected_answer "1250"
  derivation "2 litres = 2000 millilitres; 2000 - 750 = 1250"
  requirement "A quantity with a unit is converted and the arithmetic executed (plan 08 case 5, the `unit_carrying_unknown` limitation class)."
  observed "Not derived in any language. The English prompt is sent to `websearch`, two pages about similar-but-different word problems are fetched, the second returns 403, and the run ends offering an issue report. Spanish gets the unknown-language fallback."
  outcome "wrong_route"
  languages_correct "0"
self_use_expectation_honest_gap
  record_type "benchmark_expectation"
  id "honest_gap"
  plan "08"
  expected_answer "no number at all, plus the localized skill gap and its research trail"
  requirement "A verifiable-looking question whose method no trusted source supplies must produce the skill gap with a research trail and no numeric answer (plan 08 case 6)."
  observed "No number is produced, which is the required negative — but it is right by accident, not by mechanism. The reply is the same web-search capability description every other family receives, with no skill gap named and no research trail. The system does not know this question is unanswerable; it simply never got as far as answering it."
  outcome "right_negative_wrong_reason"
  languages_correct "0"
